{"page": 4, "page_size": 50, "total_matching": 248582, "total_pages": 4972, "cards_html": "\n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248432 · SUBLANGENG_Q495873</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_1CB7C975665B (Question 3 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high4104)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_1CB7C975665B · Question 3 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>In 1947 a group of famous people from the art world headed by an Austrian conductor decided to hold an intemational festival of music,dance and theatre in Edinburgh. The idea was to reunite Europe after the Second World War.</p><p>At the same time, the &quot;Fringe&quot; appeared as a challenge to the official festival.Eight theatre groups turned up uninvited in 1947,in the belief that everyone should have the right to perform,and they did so in a public house disused for years.</p><p>Soon,groups of studentsfirstly from Edinburgh University, and later from the universities of Oxford and Cambridge,Durham and Birmingham were making the journey to the Scottish capital each summer to perform theatre by little-known writers of plays in small church halls to the people of Edinburgh.</p><p>Today the &quot;Fringe&quot;,once less recognized, has far outgrown the festival with around 1,500 performances of theatre,music and dance on every one of the 21 days it lasts. And yet as early as 1959,with only 19 theatre groups performing,some said it was getting too big.</p><p>A paid administrator was first employed only in 1971, and today there are eight administrators working all year round and the number rises to 150 during August itself. In 2004 there were 200 places housing 1,695 shows by over 600 different groups from 50 different countries. More than 1,25 million tickets were sold.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Who joined the &quot;Fringe&quot; after it appeared?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">they owned a public house there</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">University students.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">rusts from around the world.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Performers of music and dance.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The core evidence lies in the passage stating that after the Fringe's appearance, 'groups of students firstly from Edinburgh University, and later from the universities of Oxford and Cambridge, Durham and Birmingham' began travelling to Edinburgh. This directly identifies university students as the group that joined later. Option A is irrelevant as ownership of a public house is never attributed to them, Option C is unmentioned with no reference to tourists from around the world, and Option D is too broad since the original Fringe groups were theatre groups rather than solely music and dance performers.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high4104) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>c7d07f7a899344a34fe9...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248431 · SUBLANGENG_Q495872</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_1CB7C975665B (Question 2 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high4104)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_1CB7C975665B · Question 2 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>In 1947 a group of famous people from the art world headed by an Austrian conductor decided to hold an intemational festival of music,dance and theatre in Edinburgh. The idea was to reunite Europe after the Second World War.</p><p>At the same time, the &quot;Fringe&quot; appeared as a challenge to the official festival.Eight theatre groups turned up uninvited in 1947,in the belief that everyone should have the right to perform,and they did so in a public house disused for years.</p><p>Soon,groups of studentsfirstly from Edinburgh University, and later from the universities of Oxford and Cambridge,Durham and Birmingham were making the journey to the Scottish capital each summer to perform theatre by little-known writers of plays in small church halls to the people of Edinburgh.</p><p>Today the &quot;Fringe&quot;,once less recognized, has far outgrown the festival with around 1,500 performances of theatre,music and dance on every one of the 21 days it lasts. And yet as early as 1959,with only 19 theatre groups performing,some said it was getting too big.</p><p>A paid administrator was first employed only in 1971, and today there are eight administrators working all year round and the number rises to 150 during August itself. In 2004 there were 200 places housing 1,695 shows by over 600 different groups from 50 different countries. More than 1,25 million tickets were sold.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Why did some uninvited theatre groups come to  Edinburgh in 1947?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">They owned a public house there.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">They came to take up a challenge.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">They thought they were also famous.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">They wanted to take part in the festival.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage clearly states that the 'Fringe' appeared as a challenge to the official festival, and the eight uninvited theatre groups acted on the belief that everyone should have the right to perform. This aligns directly with taking up that challenge, proving option B correct. Option D is false, as they came uninvited and not to enter the official festival. Options A and C are entirely unsubstantiated, with no mention of a public house owned by them or any claim of fame.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high4104) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>f995427e5509811ae341...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248430 · SUBLANGENG_Q495871</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_1CB7C975665B (Question 1 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high4104)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_1CB7C975665B · Question 1 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>In 1947 a group of famous people from the art world headed by an Austrian conductor decided to hold an intemational festival of music,dance and theatre in Edinburgh. The idea was to reunite Europe after the Second World War.</p><p>At the same time, the &quot;Fringe&quot; appeared as a challenge to the official festival.Eight theatre groups turned up uninvited in 1947,in the belief that everyone should have the right to perform,and they did so in a public house disused for years.</p><p>Soon,groups of studentsfirstly from Edinburgh University, and later from the universities of Oxford and Cambridge,Durham and Birmingham were making the journey to the Scottish capital each summer to perform theatre by little-known writers of plays in small church halls to the people of Edinburgh.</p><p>Today the &quot;Fringe&quot;,once less recognized, has far outgrown the festival with around 1,500 performances of theatre,music and dance on every one of the 21 days it lasts. And yet as early as 1959,with only 19 theatre groups performing,some said it was getting too big.</p><p>A paid administrator was first employed only in 1971, and today there are eight administrators working all year round and the number rises to 150 during August itself. In 2004 there were 200 places housing 1,695 shows by over 600 different groups from 50 different countries. More than 1,25 million tickets were sold.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Point was the purpose of Edinburgh Festival at he beginning?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">To bring Europe together again.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">To honor heroes of World War 11.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">To introduce young theatre groups.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">To attract great artists from Europe.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The key principle here is direct factual retrieval from the passage, which explicitly states that the idea behind holding the Edinburgh Festival was to reunite Europe after the Second World War. This clear motive leaves no scope for other inferences, making option A correct. Option B is baseless, as war heroes are never mentioned. Option C refers to the later Fringe movement, not the official festival's beginning. Option D is too vague and lacks any textual support.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high4104) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>526643cfbe701cf8c646...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248429 · SUBLANGENG_Q495870</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_70CC898F5E3E (Question 4 of 4)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high21220)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_70CC898F5E3E · Question 4 of 4</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Dear Earthmen ,</p><p>I have enjoyed my stay on your interesting unusual planet. I think I understand the life on earth now and I would like to give you my impressions.</p><p>First of all you live in boxes. Every morning you leave your big boxes and get into smaller boxes on wheels. All these small boxes race around and around, and finally stop to rest. You then leave these boxes on wheels and go to very large tall boxes.</p><p>After testing all days you get back in your little boxes and return to your big boxes. There you sit and stare at tiny glowing boxes with moving pictures on the front.</p><p>Only one thing puzzles me. One day I went to a football game. A bunch of angry boys fought over a little round ball. Everyone yelled for them to stop but they kept on fighting. They were angry, I suppose, about being cooped up  in boxes all day.</p><p>Thank you earthmen for this chance to get to know you.</p><p>Gratefully,</p><p>The man from the Mars</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The man from the Mars thinks  _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">it interesting to experience a lot on our unusual planet</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">there are so many boxes on the earth</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the tiny glowing boxes are moving pictures</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the angry boys are too foolish to fight over a little round ball</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The core passage evidence lies in the Martian's opening remarks, where he states he has enjoyed his stay on your 'interesting unusual planet' and wants to give his impressions. This directly reflects his overall positive view, proving option A correct. Option B is only a description of his observations of boxes, not his opinion. Options C and D are either isolated facts or drawn from the truncated football incident, neither of which represent his general impression of Earth.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high21220) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>39949e04c521397fbdb8...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248428 · SUBLANGENG_Q495869</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_70CC898F5E3E (Question 3 of 4)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high21220)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_70CC898F5E3E · Question 3 of 4</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Dear Earthmen ,</p><p>I have enjoyed my stay on your interesting unusual planet. I think I understand the life on earth now and I would like to give you my impressions.</p><p>First of all you live in boxes. Every morning you leave your big boxes and get into smaller boxes on wheels. All these small boxes race around and around, and finally stop to rest. You then leave these boxes on wheels and go to very large tall boxes.</p><p>After testing all days you get back in your little boxes and return to your big boxes. There you sit and stare at tiny glowing boxes with moving pictures on the front.</p><p>Only one thing puzzles me. One day I went to a football game. A bunch of angry boys fought over a little round ball. Everyone yelled for them to stop but they kept on fighting. They were angry, I suppose, about being cooped up  in boxes all day.</p><p>Thank you earthmen for this chance to get to know you.</p><p>Gratefully,</p><p>The man from the Mars</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The best title of this passage is  _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">The Man from the Mars</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Something about Boxes</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">A Letter from the Mars</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">A Football Game</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The core evidence lies in the epistolary form, as the entire piece begins with 'Dear Earthmen' and consists of the Martian's impressions written as a letter. This framing shows the writer is directly addressing Earthmen to share his findings. Option A overemphasizes only the character, option B is far too vague for a title, and option D would only fit a single episode. Taken together, 'A Letter from the Mars' best captures the form and purpose of the passage.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high21220) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>23df7b10a8dfbc7fb3bb...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248427 · SUBLANGENG_Q495867</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_70CC898F5E3E (Question 2 of 4)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high21220)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_70CC898F5E3E · Question 2 of 4</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Dear Earthmen ,</p><p>I have enjoyed my stay on your interesting unusual planet. I think I understand the life on earth now and I would like to give you my impressions.</p><p>First of all you live in boxes. Every morning you leave your big boxes and get into smaller boxes on wheels. All these small boxes race around and around, and finally stop to rest. You then leave these boxes on wheels and go to very large tall boxes.</p><p>After testing all days you get back in your little boxes and return to your big boxes. There you sit and stare at tiny glowing boxes with moving pictures on the front.</p><p>Only one thing puzzles me. One day I went to a football game. A bunch of angry boys fought over a little round ball. Everyone yelled for them to stop but they kept on fighting. They were angry, I suppose, about being cooped up  in boxes all day.</p><p>Thank you earthmen for this chance to get to know you.</p><p>Gratefully,</p><p>The man from the Mars</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The tiny glowing boxes with moving pictures on the front are  _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">cameras</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">cinema screens</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">TV sets</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">telescopes</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage's key phrase, 'tiny glowing boxes with moving pictures on the front', directly points to TV sets viewed in homes. By following the Martian's outsider description of domestic life, television fits as an object one would sit and stare at regularly. Option A relates to recording, option B to large public screens, and option D to viewing distant objects, none of which match the idea of moving pictures watched at home. Thus, only option C is correct.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high21220) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>9c3c303a78d57b683802...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248426 · SUBLANGENG_Q495866</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_70CC898F5E3E (Question 1 of 4)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high21220)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_70CC898F5E3E · Question 1 of 4</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Dear Earthmen ,</p><p>I have enjoyed my stay on your interesting unusual planet. I think I understand the life on earth now and I would like to give you my impressions.</p><p>First of all you live in boxes. Every morning you leave your big boxes and get into smaller boxes on wheels. All these small boxes race around and around, and finally stop to rest. You then leave these boxes on wheels and go to very large tall boxes.</p><p>After testing all days you get back in your little boxes and return to your big boxes. There you sit and stare at tiny glowing boxes with moving pictures on the front.</p><p>Only one thing puzzles me. One day I went to a football game. A bunch of angry boys fought over a little round ball. Everyone yelled for them to stop but they kept on fighting. They were angry, I suppose, about being cooped up  in boxes all day.</p><p>Thank you earthmen for this chance to get to know you.</p><p>Gratefully,</p><p>The man from the Mars</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The small boxes on wheels are  _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">toys</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">ears</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">houses that can be moved</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">boxes in which there are wheels</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>From the alien narrator's literal description, vehicles are seen purely by their outer form rather than their function. The phrase 'smaller boxes on wheels' refers to cars, and option D directly states them to be 'boxes in which there are wheels', matching this outsider's mechanical view. Options A, B and C rely on human associations such as toys, ears or movable houses, all of which ignore the exact physical description the narrator uses throughout his observation.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high21220) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>d3bd3a39c222c811db01...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248425 · SUBLANGENG_Q495863</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_F90F5CF78E12 (Question 1 of 1)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high3337)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_F90F5CF78E12 · Question 1 of 1</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A 16-year-old South Dakota boy who became lost while hunting and spent 16 hours alone in the Black Hills National Forest says he was scared but still managed to make a survival plan.</p><p>Austin DuVall, of Rapid City, became lost on Nov.3 while hunting with his father. He ran after a deer, and soon found himself alone. &quot;I ran after a deer, but I didn&#x27;t get it,&quot; he said. &quot;Then I was really lost.&quot;</p><p>He had only his hunting rifle  and the clothes he was wearing. He had no food or water and had nothing that could help him find his way to safety. &quot;I knew that no one could hear me. I decided to just sleep and get up in the morning and find safety,&quot; he said.</p><p>Austin climbed up on a rock and slept through the night. Then he awoke and relied on skills he learned in a hunter safety course. He followed a stream to an occupied cabin. The couple there called his parents and cooked him a breakfast. &quot; It&#x27;s probably one meal I&#x27;ll never forget for the rest of my life,&quot; he said.</p><p>After DuVall&#x27;s disappearance, a lot of emergency officials and more than 100 volunteers went searching for him. &quot;He wasn&#x27;t sitting there waiting for someone to come and find him,&quot; said his father, Steve DuVall. &quot;We didn&#x27;t find him; he found himself.&quot;</p><p>Mike Kintigh, regional supervisor for the Game, Fish &amp; Parks Department, said one or two hunters will go missing each year, but rarely for more than 24 hours. &quot;We&#x27;re a little bit unique in the Black Hills as it&#x27;s hard to get lost for a very long time. That&#x27;s because we&#x27;ve got so many roads here compared to the Rocky Mountains,&quot; Kintigh said. &quot;You can certainly spend a very uncomfortable night in the woods like Austin did.&quot;</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>After Austin realized he lost his way, he   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">was very nervous but excited</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">cried aloud for help</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">tried to find a safe place</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">decided to sleep in the wild</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage follows a logical course of action under duress. After realizing no one could hear him and that he was lost, Austin states his decision to just sleep and get up in the morning to find safety. This direct piece of evidence points to Option D. Option A is contradicted by his fear, B has no support in the text, and C is incorrect as he does not actively search at that moment, but instead resolves to rest before searching the next day.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high3337) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>48b5ee5c93764a78aabd...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248424 · SUBLANGENG_Q495862</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_6FF33A49E55E (Question 3 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high21742)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_6FF33A49E55E · Question 3 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>This girl is almost without shelter. She may not realize it, but she&#x27;s more exposed to the world than she&#x27;s ever likely to be again. And it isn&#x27;t because she&#x27;s a girl. It could be a boy. It could be you.</p><p>But why is she &#x27;shelter less ? She s got a place to live in quite a pleasant place by the look of it and if shelter .</p><p>Doesn&#x27;t&#x27; t mean a house, then what does it mean? When we say someone &quot;lives a sheltered life&quot; , we don&#x27;t only mean that their house is comfortable. We mean that they&#x27;re protected from too many worries and troubles, that they live in a settled home, probably surrounded by friends and family, and that they don&#x27;t have to cope with the difficulties the world is full of alone.</p><p>Certainly no one would say that this girl was leading a sheltered life; she&#x27;s leaving home to earn her living in a strange city and live by herself in a bed sitter. She may be just as well protected physically as a &quot;sheltered life&quot; person, but she&#x27;s lost all the other shelters in her life--family, friends, the home she grew up in, school, the groups she belonged to. She s on her own now and unless she&#x27;s very self-reliant , she&#x27;s likely to feel unhappy and insecure at times.</p><p>A young person setting out on her own like this is between the two main kinds of shelter most of us spend our lives in. One is our parents home where we grow up, and the other is the home we make ourselves and where we bring up our own children. For most people the time they spend between or outside these two shelters is only a small part of their lives.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>What would be best title for the passage?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Leaving Home</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Finding a House</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Living with the Family</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Making a Better Shelter</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage's central theme is the contrast between literal shelter and true protection. By opening with a seemingly 'shelterless' girl in a pleasant home, the author draws attention to the vulnerability of leaving or lacking a sheltered life. This idea of exposure closely aligns with the concept of leaving home and losing that protection. Option A reflects this. B is far too narrow, C is not addressed at all, and D shifts focus to 'making' shelter rather than the vulnerability created by its absence.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high21742) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>2ec200161c8918626475...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248423 · SUBLANGENG_Q495861</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_6FF33A49E55E (Question 2 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high21742)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_6FF33A49E55E · Question 2 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>This girl is almost without shelter. She may not realize it, but she&#x27;s more exposed to the world than she&#x27;s ever likely to be again. And it isn&#x27;t because she&#x27;s a girl. It could be a boy. It could be you.</p><p>But why is she &#x27;shelter less ? She s got a place to live in quite a pleasant place by the look of it and if shelter .</p><p>Doesn&#x27;t&#x27; t mean a house, then what does it mean? When we say someone &quot;lives a sheltered life&quot; , we don&#x27;t only mean that their house is comfortable. We mean that they&#x27;re protected from too many worries and troubles, that they live in a settled home, probably surrounded by friends and family, and that they don&#x27;t have to cope with the difficulties the world is full of alone.</p><p>Certainly no one would say that this girl was leading a sheltered life; she&#x27;s leaving home to earn her living in a strange city and live by herself in a bed sitter. She may be just as well protected physically as a &quot;sheltered life&quot; person, but she&#x27;s lost all the other shelters in her life--family, friends, the home she grew up in, school, the groups she belonged to. She s on her own now and unless she&#x27;s very self-reliant , she&#x27;s likely to feel unhappy and insecure at times.</p><p>A young person setting out on her own like this is between the two main kinds of shelter most of us spend our lives in. One is our parents home where we grow up, and the other is the home we make ourselves and where we bring up our own children. For most people the time they spend between or outside these two shelters is only a small part of their lives.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>When we say someone &quot;lives a sheltered life&quot;, we mean they   _   .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">live in the country</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">have a comfortable house</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">don t have any worries</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">have a secure home life and don t have to face problems alone</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The idiom 'lives a sheltered life' relies on contextual meaning, not the literal word 'house'. The passage explicitly states that it refers to being protected from too many worries and troubles, living in a settled home, being surrounded by friends and family, and not having to cope alone. Option D combines all of these ideas precisely. By contrast, A is location-based, B only focuses on a comfortable house, and C is an overstatement as the phrase implies protection rather than a complete absence of any worries.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high21742) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>f580ce6cb04990685c1f...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248422 · SUBLANGENG_Q495860</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_6FF33A49E55E (Question 1 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high21742)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_6FF33A49E55E · Question 1 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>This girl is almost without shelter. She may not realize it, but she&#x27;s more exposed to the world than she&#x27;s ever likely to be again. And it isn&#x27;t because she&#x27;s a girl. It could be a boy. It could be you.</p><p>But why is she &#x27;shelter less ? She s got a place to live in quite a pleasant place by the look of it and if shelter .</p><p>Doesn&#x27;t&#x27; t mean a house, then what does it mean? When we say someone &quot;lives a sheltered life&quot; , we don&#x27;t only mean that their house is comfortable. We mean that they&#x27;re protected from too many worries and troubles, that they live in a settled home, probably surrounded by friends and family, and that they don&#x27;t have to cope with the difficulties the world is full of alone.</p><p>Certainly no one would say that this girl was leading a sheltered life; she&#x27;s leaving home to earn her living in a strange city and live by herself in a bed sitter. She may be just as well protected physically as a &quot;sheltered life&quot; person, but she&#x27;s lost all the other shelters in her life--family, friends, the home she grew up in, school, the groups she belonged to. She s on her own now and unless she&#x27;s very self-reliant , she&#x27;s likely to feel unhappy and insecure at times.</p><p>A young person setting out on her own like this is between the two main kinds of shelter most of us spend our lives in. One is our parents home where we grow up, and the other is the home we make ourselves and where we bring up our own children. For most people the time they spend between or outside these two shelters is only a small part of their lives.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>It can be inferred from the passage that this girl   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">has nowhere to live</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">will have problems because she&#x27;s a girl</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">is probably going to feel lonely</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">wants to live in her home again</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The key principle here is the passage's distinction between a physical house and the meaning of 'shelter', as 'living a sheltered life' denotes protection from worries, a settled home, support from friends and family, and freedom from having to cope alone. Applying this, the girl being 'almost without shelter' and 'more exposed to the world' means she lacks that protective environment. This strongly points to isolation and loneliness, making C correct. A is false as no home-loss is stated, B is unprovable by gender alone, and D is pure conjecture with no textual basis.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high21742) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>b61527d6c8f963b7f413...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248421 · SUBLANGENG_Q495857</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_7C19F02F3C37 (Question 2 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high9123)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_7C19F02F3C37 · Question 2 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Three Central Texas men were honored with the Texas Department of Public Safety&#x27;s Director&#x27;s Award in a Tuesday morning ceremony for their heroism in saving the victims of a fiery two car accident.</p><p>The accident occurred on March 25 when a vehicle lost control while traveling on a rain-soaked State Highway 6 near Baylor Camp Road. It ran into an oncoming vehicle, leaving the occupants trapped inside as both vehicles burst into flames.</p><p>Bonge was the first on the scene and heard children screaming. He broke through a back window and pulled Mallory Smith, 10, and her sister, Megan Smith,9,from the wreckage.</p><p>The girls&#x27; mother, Beckie Smith, was not with them at the time of the wreck, as they were traveling with their baby sitter, Lisa Bow bin.</p><p>Beckie Smith still remembers the sickening feeling she had up on receiving the call informing her of the wreck and the despair as she drove to the scene.</p><p>Bozeman and Clemmons arrived shortly after Bonge and helped rescue the other victims and attempted to put out the fires.</p><p>&quot;I was nervous,&quot; Bozeman said.&quot; I don&#x27;t feel like I&#x27;m a hero. I was just doing what anyone should do in that situation. I hope someone would do the same for me.&quot;</p><p>Everyone at the accident made it out alive, with the victims suffering from nonlife-threatening injuries. Mallory Smith broke both femurs, and Megan had neck and back injuries. Bowbin is still recovering from a broken pelvis, ankle and foot.</p><p>The rescuers also were taken to the hospital and treated for cuts and smoke breathing, Bonge said.</p><p>In addition, Bozeman not to meet accident victim Anthony Rus so in the hospital after the accident, where Russo presented him with a glass frame inscribed with&quot; Thank you,&quot; Bozeman said. Those involved in that fateful encounter on Highway 6 credited God blessing for bringing them together.</p><p>&quot;Whatever the circumstances, Tuesday&#x27;s ceremony provided a time to be grateful for those who put their lives on the line for the lives of complete strangers,&quot; Beckie Smith said,&quot; We&#x27;re calling it The Miracle on Highway 6.&quot;</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>What&#x27;s the main idea of the passage?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Three persons were awarded for rescuing victims in a car accident.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Three ordinary people were regarded as great heroes.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Several victims were carried to safety from the burning cars.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">A car accident occurred on a rain-soaked State Highway 6.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage's central focus is the honoring of three Central Texas men with the Texas Department of Public Safety's Director's Award for their heroism in rescuing the victims of a fiery two-car accident. This ceremony and the act of award-giving, rather than the weather or the crash alone, form the unifying idea of the report. Options B and C are too general to cover all three men, while option D states only a peripheral detail of when and where the crash occurred. Accordingly, only option A captures the passage's main idea with full textual support.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high9123) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>66fdbe40396f975a699b...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248420 · SUBLANGENG_Q495856</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_7C19F02F3C37 (Question 1 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high9123)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_7C19F02F3C37 · Question 1 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Three Central Texas men were honored with the Texas Department of Public Safety&#x27;s Director&#x27;s Award in a Tuesday morning ceremony for their heroism in saving the victims of a fiery two car accident.</p><p>The accident occurred on March 25 when a vehicle lost control while traveling on a rain-soaked State Highway 6 near Baylor Camp Road. It ran into an oncoming vehicle, leaving the occupants trapped inside as both vehicles burst into flames.</p><p>Bonge was the first on the scene and heard children screaming. He broke through a back window and pulled Mallory Smith, 10, and her sister, Megan Smith,9,from the wreckage.</p><p>The girls&#x27; mother, Beckie Smith, was not with them at the time of the wreck, as they were traveling with their baby sitter, Lisa Bow bin.</p><p>Beckie Smith still remembers the sickening feeling she had up on receiving the call informing her of the wreck and the despair as she drove to the scene.</p><p>Bozeman and Clemmons arrived shortly after Bonge and helped rescue the other victims and attempted to put out the fires.</p><p>&quot;I was nervous,&quot; Bozeman said.&quot; I don&#x27;t feel like I&#x27;m a hero. I was just doing what anyone should do in that situation. I hope someone would do the same for me.&quot;</p><p>Everyone at the accident made it out alive, with the victims suffering from nonlife-threatening injuries. Mallory Smith broke both femurs, and Megan had neck and back injuries. Bowbin is still recovering from a broken pelvis, ankle and foot.</p><p>The rescuers also were taken to the hospital and treated for cuts and smoke breathing, Bonge said.</p><p>In addition, Bozeman not to meet accident victim Anthony Rus so in the hospital after the accident, where Russo presented him with a glass frame inscribed with&quot; Thank you,&quot; Bozeman said. Those involved in that fateful encounter on Highway 6 credited God blessing for bringing them together.</p><p>&quot;Whatever the circumstances, Tuesday&#x27;s ceremony provided a time to be grateful for those who put their lives on the line for the lives of complete strangers,&quot; Beckie Smith said,&quot; We&#x27;re calling it The Miracle on Highway 6.&quot;</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Who saved Megan Smith from the damaged car?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Clemmons.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Anthony Russo.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Bozeman.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Bonge.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The core passage evidence states that Bonge was the first on the scene, heard the children screaming, broke through a back window, and pulled both Mallory Smith and Megan Smith from the wreckage. By direct textual mapping, this action is explicitly attributed to Bonge alone for Megan's rescue. The other names appear only as distractors with no act of extraction assigned to them in the given text, and none are linked to breaking into the burning vehicle to save Megan. Thus, only option D is conclusively proven.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high9123) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>0373d1b06d5e0318e459...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248419 · SUBLANGENG_Q495851</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_CB0B66CA59ED (Question 1 of 1)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high10525)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_CB0B66CA59ED · Question 1 of 1</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>If you go into the woods with your friends, stay with them. If you don&#x27;t, you may get lost. If you do get lost, this is what you should do.</p><p>Sit down and stay where you are. Don&#x27;t try to find your friends -- let them find you. You can help them to find you by staying in one place.</p><p>There is another way to help your friends or other people nearby to find you. Give them a signal by shouting or whistling three times. Stop. Then shout or whistle three times again. Any signal given three times is a call for help. You will be helped by others.</p><p>Keep up the shouting or whistling, always three times together. When people hear you, they will know that you are not just making noise for fun. They will let you know they have heard your signal. They will give two shouts, two whistles or two gunshots. When a signal is given twice, it is an answer to a call for help.</p><p>If you don&#x27;t think that you will get help before night comes, try to make a little house and cover up the holes with branches with lots of leaves and grass. What should you do if you get hungry or need to drink some water? You should have to leave your little branch house to look for a brook. Don&#x27;t just walk away. Pick off small branches and drop them as you walk so that you can find your way back.</p><p>The most important thing to do when you are lost is -- stay in one place.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>How do you let people believe that you are not just making noise for fun?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Stop now and then.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Go on shouting or whistling.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Shout over and over at the top of voice.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Shout or whistle three times once a while.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The guiding principle here is the stated rule that 'Any signal given three times is a call for help'. Applying this to the instructions, the passage tells the lost person to shout or whistle three times, stop, and then do it again to attract attention. Option D reflects this exact pattern of giving the three-time signal at intervals to be recognised as distress. Option A is too vague, B implies constant noise with no distinction, and C suggests reckless shouting with no set pattern, all of which fail to show the deliberate three-time call that tells others it is not aimless noise.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high10525) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>6babab352d4790bef771...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248418 · SUBLANGENG_Q495849</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_79D5D6EDE02E (Question 2 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high10339)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_79D5D6EDE02E · Question 2 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Winter is the time of year when people feel very blessed. This isn&#x27;t because people feel thankful for the cold weather, nor because the important festivals---Christmas or Spring Festival---offer an excuse to celebrate. In fact, &quot;Bless you!&quot; is a common response if someone sneezes, a symptom of catching a cold or the flu.</p><p>Colds and the flu are the most common illnesses of autumn and winter as the weather gets colder. Viruses cause them. If you get one you will feel annoyed, but it is not usually serious. The flu is spread from person to person when we come into contact with a person with the virus. We get the virus on our hands and then we touch our noses and our mouths. We can pass on the flu before we realize we have it. You can infect  others one day before symptoms develop and for up to five days after becoming sick.</p><p>Getting a flu vaccination is the best way to prevent the illness. Even if your body has built up antibodies for one kind of flu. The vaccine is only effective for one year and viruses are different from year to year, so it is necessary to get a flu vaccination every year. The best time to get the vaccination is October or November. Besides, there are other ways to reduce your chance of getting a flu. Wash your hands. Get enough rest. Eat garlic regularly. Don&#x27;t let stress control you. Exercise regularly.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The passage is intended to tell us   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">how to keep healthy .</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the causes of flu .</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the influence of flu .</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">what to do about flu.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The core evidence from the passage is that colds and the flu are caused by viruses and spread from person to person through contact. Tracing the text, the author first explains why people say 'Bless you!' and then states the origin and mode of transmission, with no practical advice given at all. Option B directly matches this focus on causation. By contrast, A, C and D all suggest actions, outcomes or remedies that are never mentioned, making them incorrect since the passage aims to explain the cause of the flu rather than tell the reader what to do about it.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high10339) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>f54230b11b5dd215d490...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248417 · SUBLANGENG_Q495847</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_79D5D6EDE02E (Question 1 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high10339)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_79D5D6EDE02E · Question 1 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Winter is the time of year when people feel very blessed. This isn&#x27;t because people feel thankful for the cold weather, nor because the important festivals---Christmas or Spring Festival---offer an excuse to celebrate. In fact, &quot;Bless you!&quot; is a common response if someone sneezes, a symptom of catching a cold or the flu.</p><p>Colds and the flu are the most common illnesses of autumn and winter as the weather gets colder. Viruses cause them. If you get one you will feel annoyed, but it is not usually serious. The flu is spread from person to person when we come into contact with a person with the virus. We get the virus on our hands and then we touch our noses and our mouths. We can pass on the flu before we realize we have it. You can infect  others one day before symptoms develop and for up to five days after becoming sick.</p><p>Getting a flu vaccination is the best way to prevent the illness. Even if your body has built up antibodies for one kind of flu. The vaccine is only effective for one year and viruses are different from year to year, so it is necessary to get a flu vaccination every year. The best time to get the vaccination is October or November. Besides, there are other ways to reduce your chance of getting a flu. Wash your hands. Get enough rest. Eat garlic regularly. Don&#x27;t let stress control you. Exercise regularly.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>We say &quot;Bless you!&quot; when   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">we feel annoyed at someone.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">someone sneezes.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">someone catches a cold or the flu.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">we celebrate some important festivals.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage gives explicit evidence stating, \"'Bless you!' is a common response if someone sneezes, a symptom of catching a cold or the flu.\" Following this direct statement, sneezing is the trigger for the phrase. Option A is wrong as annoyance is a reaction to illness, not the cue. Option C confuses the symptom-cause with the act, and Option D wrongly links it to festivals. Only B matches the exact passage evidence, making it correct.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high10339) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>02de6a7a7afa89cd4b0e...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248416 · SUBLANGENG_Q495846</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_DFD6D45FB6C3 (Question 2 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high18079)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_DFD6D45FB6C3 · Question 2 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Any high school students lucky enough to be accepted to Harvard University can easily count themselves among the country&#x27;s best and brightest.</p><p>The story of David Boone&#x27;s journey from sleeping on a park bench to one of Harvard&#x27;s dorm rooms, certainly stands out from the crowd of his peers.</p><p>David, a 17-year-old senior at a MC2 Stem, a high school in Cleveland, Ohio that focuses largely on engineering and science classes with the help of a grant   from the Bill and Melinda Gates Foundation, was offered a full-ride scholarship to Harvard in the fall.</p><p>His family life has been complicated for the past few years after gangs and economic hardships resulted in him being separated from his family and forced to look after himself on the streets and park benches in Cleveland.</p><p>Because both his grandmother and mother could not afford to house the teenagers, his siblings split up to stay with various family friends, but because of space issues and his allergies   to the families pets, David was unable to stay. He ended up in the safer neighborhood of Coventry where there was a safer park with fewer dangers.</p><p>&quot;All of these life lessons have shaped me into who I am, transforming my dreams and aspirations and allowing me to free myself from what was becoming an unproductive environment,&quot; he wrote in his blog post.</p><p>David&#x27;s thirst for knowledge had never been reduced and his enthusiasm for engineering and science was growing. A short while later, Jeff McClellan, the principal of MC2 Stem was immediately impressed by David&#x27;s dedication in the face of adversity, as well as his academic talent.</p><p>&quot;Here&#x27;s a kid who&#x27;s doing everything in his power to get where he wants to go and we had the available resources to provide a little additional support, &quot;Mr McClellan told the local ABC News.</p><p>At MC2 Stem, David found the exact fit, where it seems he was born to absorb what they were offering. Principal Jeff McClellan found David to be a great student and all-around person, but with a serious living situation, so he stepped in to help. After a home discussion with his wife, McClellan decided to offer David a place to live until he could find another home. Mr McClellan and his wife took the teen in and helped him before he found a permanent solution.</p><p>When it came to his next step, David aimed high and applied for a list of top colleges, including the University of Pennsylvania, MIT, Princeton, Cornell, Yale, Harvard and Washington University in St. Louis. In the end, only MIT rejected his application and he was left to choose his own fate from the selective prestigious and mostly Ivy League schools.</p><p>David&#x27;s next challenge is to fight back tears at graduation this weekend. &quot;I promised myself I wouldn&#x27;t cry. But I realize that&#x27;s what everyone does before they cry. I&#x27;m pretty sure there&#x27;s going to be a lot of emotion there.&quot; he said.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>What&#x27;s probably the best title for the passage?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Chances are there, making an effort to seize them</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Deal with adversity, being determined</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Best way to experience, choosing to be homeless</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">From a park bench to a Harvard dormitory An incredible story</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The core principle of a title is to encapsulate the passage's central theme. The text traces David Boone's journey from sleeping on a park bench to earning a full-ride scholarship to Harvard. Option D directly reflects this rise from hardship to triumph. Option A is too vague, Option B ignores the Harvard outcome, and Option C is factually absurd as homelessness is a misfortune, not a recommended experience. Thus, D is the only option that fully captures the passage's arc.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high18079) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>b239116bf77a16ea065e...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248415 · SUBLANGENG_Q495844</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_DFD6D45FB6C3 (Question 1 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high18079)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_DFD6D45FB6C3 · Question 1 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Any high school students lucky enough to be accepted to Harvard University can easily count themselves among the country&#x27;s best and brightest.</p><p>The story of David Boone&#x27;s journey from sleeping on a park bench to one of Harvard&#x27;s dorm rooms, certainly stands out from the crowd of his peers.</p><p>David, a 17-year-old senior at a MC2 Stem, a high school in Cleveland, Ohio that focuses largely on engineering and science classes with the help of a grant   from the Bill and Melinda Gates Foundation, was offered a full-ride scholarship to Harvard in the fall.</p><p>His family life has been complicated for the past few years after gangs and economic hardships resulted in him being separated from his family and forced to look after himself on the streets and park benches in Cleveland.</p><p>Because both his grandmother and mother could not afford to house the teenagers, his siblings split up to stay with various family friends, but because of space issues and his allergies   to the families pets, David was unable to stay. He ended up in the safer neighborhood of Coventry where there was a safer park with fewer dangers.</p><p>&quot;All of these life lessons have shaped me into who I am, transforming my dreams and aspirations and allowing me to free myself from what was becoming an unproductive environment,&quot; he wrote in his blog post.</p><p>David&#x27;s thirst for knowledge had never been reduced and his enthusiasm for engineering and science was growing. A short while later, Jeff McClellan, the principal of MC2 Stem was immediately impressed by David&#x27;s dedication in the face of adversity, as well as his academic talent.</p><p>&quot;Here&#x27;s a kid who&#x27;s doing everything in his power to get where he wants to go and we had the available resources to provide a little additional support, &quot;Mr McClellan told the local ABC News.</p><p>At MC2 Stem, David found the exact fit, where it seems he was born to absorb what they were offering. Principal Jeff McClellan found David to be a great student and all-around person, but with a serious living situation, so he stepped in to help. After a home discussion with his wife, McClellan decided to offer David a place to live until he could find another home. Mr McClellan and his wife took the teen in and helped him before he found a permanent solution.</p><p>When it came to his next step, David aimed high and applied for a list of top colleges, including the University of Pennsylvania, MIT, Princeton, Cornell, Yale, Harvard and Washington University in St. Louis. In the end, only MIT rejected his application and he was left to choose his own fate from the selective prestigious and mostly Ivy League schools.</p><p>David&#x27;s next challenge is to fight back tears at graduation this weekend. &quot;I promised myself I wouldn&#x27;t cry. But I realize that&#x27;s what everyone does before they cry. I&#x27;m pretty sure there&#x27;s going to be a lot of emotion there.&quot; he said.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Jeff McClellan was impressed by David&#x27;s   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">honesty and sincerity</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">positive attitude towards life</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">courage when facing difficulties</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">great academic achievement</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Jeff McClellan was impressed by David's courage when facing difficulties, as evidenced by David's journey from sleeping on a park bench to being accepted into Harvard. David's honesty, positive attitude, and academic achievements are mentioned, but the passage highlights his courage most directly.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high18079) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>0341d987c5732e149b90...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248414 · SUBLANGENG_Q495842</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_426ACA2118AC (Question 3 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high15185)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_426ACA2118AC · Question 3 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Welcome to Coteborg University</p><p>Coteborg University is one of Sweden&#x27;s largest and most popular universities.</p><p>We are very proud of this and believe that there are several reasons for our popularity. The principal reasons we believe to be the high quality of our education and research and the broad range of courses that we offer. In addition to this, Coteborg University provides an attractive and exceptionally high-standard study environment. Most parts of the university are situated in the city centre and this enriches city life as well as student life.</p><p>Coteborg has a lot to offer its students: it has a rich and varied cultural life with many theatres, concerts and festivals. For those looking for outdoor life, forests and vast recreation areas are not far away from the city centre; the sea and the archipelago are also within easy reach. Industry and commerce are expanding, and have a joint interest with the University in meeting the ever-changing and growing demands of society.</p><p>Coteborg University strives to be an attractive choice for students from all over the world.</p><p>We look forward to welcoming you to Coteborg University.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>What&#x27;s the main purpose of this passage?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">To bring fame to Coteborg University.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">To introduce the wonderful cultural life in Coteborg University.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">To declare Coteborg University&#x27;s goal and interest.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">To attract students all over the world to apply for Coteborg University.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage adopts an informative welcome by highlighting the university's strengths, such as teaching, research, courses, study environment, location and cultural offerings to promote appeal. These features are presented to showcase its value with the clear aim of drawing applicants from elsewhere, which matches option D. Option A is too vague, option B is only one minor aspect, and option C misrepresents the text by suggesting a declared goal or interest rather than a promotional introduction.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high15185) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>d7da5b5aeaec56ce98a3...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248413 · SUBLANGENG_Q495841</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_426ACA2118AC (Question 2 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high15185)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_426ACA2118AC · Question 2 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Welcome to Coteborg University</p><p>Coteborg University is one of Sweden&#x27;s largest and most popular universities.</p><p>We are very proud of this and believe that there are several reasons for our popularity. The principal reasons we believe to be the high quality of our education and research and the broad range of courses that we offer. In addition to this, Coteborg University provides an attractive and exceptionally high-standard study environment. Most parts of the university are situated in the city centre and this enriches city life as well as student life.</p><p>Coteborg has a lot to offer its students: it has a rich and varied cultural life with many theatres, concerts and festivals. For those looking for outdoor life, forests and vast recreation areas are not far away from the city centre; the sea and the archipelago are also within easy reach. Industry and commerce are expanding, and have a joint interest with the University in meeting the ever-changing and growing demands of society.</p><p>Coteborg University strives to be an attractive choice for students from all over the world.</p><p>We look forward to welcoming you to Coteborg University.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Which of the following statements is true?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">The university is in the city centre.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">The students can live outdoor.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">The cultural life of the university is very rich.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">The University has no interest in growing demands of society.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The core evidence comes from the statement that most parts of the university are situated in the city centre, a fact that directly supports option A. This locational detail is clearly given, so the claim holds true as stated. Option B is pure speculation about outdoor living, option C refers to Coteborg's wider cultural life rather than a stated fact exclusive to the university, and option D is contradicted by the passage's focus on the university's positive appeal.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high15185) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>b3676520f5a84c04407b...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248412 · SUBLANGENG_Q495840</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_426ACA2118AC (Question 1 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high15185)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_426ACA2118AC · Question 1 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Welcome to Coteborg University</p><p>Coteborg University is one of Sweden&#x27;s largest and most popular universities.</p><p>We are very proud of this and believe that there are several reasons for our popularity. The principal reasons we believe to be the high quality of our education and research and the broad range of courses that we offer. In addition to this, Coteborg University provides an attractive and exceptionally high-standard study environment. Most parts of the university are situated in the city centre and this enriches city life as well as student life.</p><p>Coteborg has a lot to offer its students: it has a rich and varied cultural life with many theatres, concerts and festivals. For those looking for outdoor life, forests and vast recreation areas are not far away from the city centre; the sea and the archipelago are also within easy reach. Industry and commerce are expanding, and have a joint interest with the University in meeting the ever-changing and growing demands of society.</p><p>Coteborg University strives to be an attractive choice for students from all over the world.</p><p>We look forward to welcoming you to Coteborg University.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The main reasons for Coteborg University&#x27;s popularity according to the passage is   _   .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the high quality education and research and the wide range of courses</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the convenient traffic</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">its excellent location and fast developing economical environment</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">famous professors and friendly students</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage explicitly states that the principal reasons for Coteborg University's popularity are the high quality of its education and research and the broad range of courses it offers. This exact pairing is reflected in option A, making it directly verifiable from the text. Options B and C introduce traffic or economic factors never mentioned, while D wrongly attributes popularity to famous professors and friendly students with no textual evidence to support either claim.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high15185) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>f55f53dadc143339cb6d...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248411 · SUBLANGENG_Q495837</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_EB7EAC39593A (Question 2 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high11841)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_EB7EAC39593A · Question 2 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Ariau Amazon Towers</p><p>The Ariau Amazon Towers hotel lets you sleep in a tree house. Eight towers make up this hotel that offers over 300 rooms. If you really want to get into the spirit, book the Tarzan Suite which is large enough for a big family. You&#x27;ll be thirty feet up in the air and can travel between the towers through their wooden walkways.</p><p>Prices: starting at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>300 one night for each person for a regular room and going all the way up to </mi></mrow></math>3000 for the Tarzan Suite.</p><p>For more information, visit the website: http://www.ariautowers.com</p><p>The Ice Hotel</p><p>Every winter in Jukkasjarvi, Sweden, a special kind of hotel called the Ice Hotel is built. Each year, world-famous artists are invited to design and produce works of art from the ice, many of which can be found in the rooms. You&#x27;ll have your choice between hot or cold rooms, but you will be well advised to stay at least one night in a cold room for a true experience.</p><p>Prices: starting at USD 318 one night for each person for either a cold room or a warm one.</p><p>For more information, visit the website: http://www.icehotel.com</p><p>Propeller Island</p><p>Propeller Island City Lodge is a very special hotel that was designed by a German artist. Each room provides you with the possibility of living in a work of art. Every single piece of furniture in the thirty rooms of the hotel has been hand-made and each room is completely different. You&#x27;ll be able to choose a room based on your own personal tastes.</p><p>Prices: starting at just USD 91 a night, and an additional person for only 20 extra dollars.</p><p>For more information, visit the website: http://www.propeller-island.com</p><p>For information about other cool hotels in the world, visit the website:</p><p>http://www.bahamabeachclub.com</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>For two persons spending a night in one of these hotels, they have to pay at least   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">USD 111</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">USD 182</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">USD 600</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">USD 636</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The core evidence from the passage is that the Ariau Amazon Towers offers regular rooms starting at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn></math> one night for each person. Applying this rate, two persons would pay at least <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x00D7;</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>600</mn></math>. Options A and B fall far below this stated minimum, while option D exceeds the minimum rate. Only option C matches the product derived directly from the passage, making it the correct and provable answer.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high11841) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>8664c30a28fbea10a154...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248410 · SUBLANGENG_Q495836</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_EB7EAC39593A (Question 1 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high11841)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_EB7EAC39593A · Question 1 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Ariau Amazon Towers</p><p>The Ariau Amazon Towers hotel lets you sleep in a tree house. Eight towers make up this hotel that offers over 300 rooms. If you really want to get into the spirit, book the Tarzan Suite which is large enough for a big family. You&#x27;ll be thirty feet up in the air and can travel between the towers through their wooden walkways.</p><p>Prices: starting at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>300 one night for each person for a regular room and going all the way up to </mi></mrow></math>3000 for the Tarzan Suite.</p><p>For more information, visit the website: http://www.ariautowers.com</p><p>The Ice Hotel</p><p>Every winter in Jukkasjarvi, Sweden, a special kind of hotel called the Ice Hotel is built. Each year, world-famous artists are invited to design and produce works of art from the ice, many of which can be found in the rooms. You&#x27;ll have your choice between hot or cold rooms, but you will be well advised to stay at least one night in a cold room for a true experience.</p><p>Prices: starting at USD 318 one night for each person for either a cold room or a warm one.</p><p>For more information, visit the website: http://www.icehotel.com</p><p>Propeller Island</p><p>Propeller Island City Lodge is a very special hotel that was designed by a German artist. Each room provides you with the possibility of living in a work of art. Every single piece of furniture in the thirty rooms of the hotel has been hand-made and each room is completely different. You&#x27;ll be able to choose a room based on your own personal tastes.</p><p>Prices: starting at just USD 91 a night, and an additional person for only 20 extra dollars.</p><p>For more information, visit the website: http://www.propeller-island.com</p><p>For information about other cool hotels in the world, visit the website:</p><p>http://www.bahamabeachclub.com</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>What is special about the Ariau Amazon Towers hotel?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">You can sleep in tree houses.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">You can choose any of the towers.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">It is designed for big families.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Every room has a walkway.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage directly states that the Ariau Amazon Towers hotel lets you sleep in a tree house. This is its defining feature, supported by the mention of towers and wooden walkways connecting them. Option A matches this evidence exactly, while B is false as you book rooms, C is an exaggeration from the Tarzan Suite, and D is incorrect since not every room has a walkway mentioned.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high11841) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>7a135b3bcbf2a4317f8d...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248409 · SUBLANGENG_Q495835</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_22E2BBD238D2 (Question 3 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high4834)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_22E2BBD238D2 · Question 3 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>The United States is full of cars. There are still many families without cars, but some families have two or more. However, cars are used for more than pleasure. They are a necessary part of life.</p><p>Cars are used for business. They are driven to offices and factories by workers who have no other way to get to their jobs. When salesmen are sent to different parts of the city, they have to drive in order to carry their products. Farmers have to drive into the city in order to get supplies.</p><p>Sometimes small children must be driven to school. In some cities school buses are used only when children live more than a mile away from the school. When the children are too young to walk too far, their mothers take turns driving them to school. One mother drives on Mondays taking her own children and the neighbors&#x27; as well. Another mother drives on Tuesdays, another on Wednesday, and so on. This is called forming a car pool. Men also form car pools, with three or four men taking turns driving to the place where they all work.</p><p>More car pools should be formed in order to put fewer cars on the road and use less gas. Too many cars are being driven. Something will have to be done about the use of cars.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The traffic in and around cities is a great problem because  _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">too many cars are being driven</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">there are too many car pools</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">people put fewer cars on the roads</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">there is less gas</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage builds on the fact that the United States is full of cars and that they are a necessity for work, farming, sales, and school runs. With so many cars being used for daily life, the natural result is heavy traffic in and around cities. Option A reflects this cause, while B is not stated as a problem, C is the opposite, and D mentions gas which has no link to traffic volume here.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high4834) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>2331e4d96231b5e5e88b...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248408 · SUBLANGENG_Q495834</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_22E2BBD238D2 (Question 2 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high4834)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_22E2BBD238D2 · Question 2 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>The United States is full of cars. There are still many families without cars, but some families have two or more. However, cars are used for more than pleasure. They are a necessary part of life.</p><p>Cars are used for business. They are driven to offices and factories by workers who have no other way to get to their jobs. When salesmen are sent to different parts of the city, they have to drive in order to carry their products. Farmers have to drive into the city in order to get supplies.</p><p>Sometimes small children must be driven to school. In some cities school buses are used only when children live more than a mile away from the school. When the children are too young to walk too far, their mothers take turns driving them to school. One mother drives on Mondays taking her own children and the neighbors&#x27; as well. Another mother drives on Tuesdays, another on Wednesday, and so on. This is called forming a car pool. Men also form car pools, with three or four men taking turns driving to the place where they all work.</p><p>More car pools should be formed in order to put fewer cars on the road and use less gas. Too many cars are being driven. Something will have to be done about the use of cars.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Mothers form car pools in order that  _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">they can drive to school</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">they can take turns driving their children to school</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">they reach school quickly</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">they can drive their children to school in time</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage states that small children must be driven to school and that school buses are used only when children live more than a mile away. A car pool is based on the principle of shared responsibility, so parents take turns driving their children. Option B fits this directly, while A and D imply a single family driving alone, and C introduces the idea of speed which is never mentioned in the text.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high4834) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>8e7c0476c6b48efc5eae...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248407 · SUBLANGENG_Q495833</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_22E2BBD238D2 (Question 1 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">COUNTRY_LOCAL: United States</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high4834)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_22E2BBD238D2 · Question 1 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>The United States is full of cars. There are still many families without cars, but some families have two or more. However, cars are used for more than pleasure. They are a necessary part of life.</p><p>Cars are used for business. They are driven to offices and factories by workers who have no other way to get to their jobs. When salesmen are sent to different parts of the city, they have to drive in order to carry their products. Farmers have to drive into the city in order to get supplies.</p><p>Sometimes small children must be driven to school. In some cities school buses are used only when children live more than a mile away from the school. When the children are too young to walk too far, their mothers take turns driving them to school. One mother drives on Mondays taking her own children and the neighbors&#x27; as well. Another mother drives on Tuesdays, another on Wednesday, and so on. This is called forming a car pool. Men also form car pools, with three or four men taking turns driving to the place where they all work.</p><p>More car pools should be formed in order to put fewer cars on the road and use less gas. Too many cars are being driven. Something will have to be done about the use of cars.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The United States is filled with cars, but  _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">not every family has a car</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">few families have two cars or even more</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">every American has a car</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">every family has a car</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage explicitly states that although the United States has many cars, many families still do not own one. This establishes that car ownership is widespread but not universal. Option A accurately expresses this contrast and is therefore correct. Option B contradicts the passage's statement that some families have two or more cars, while options C and D incorrectly claim that every American or every family owns a car.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high4834) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>804352168ad9f9a14833...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248406 · SUBLANGENG_Q495831</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_E65AA5310558 (Question 1 of 1)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high21593)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_E65AA5310558 · Question 1 of 1</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>People in Mutsuhito, Japan, lived through one hundreds, and sometimes thousands, a day.But they couldn&#x27;t get used to it.</p><p>What was it? It was a string of earthquakes that made the small town shake all the time.This went on for more than a year.Sometimes the quakes were very small.Only certain instruments could pick them up.At other times, the quakes damaged houses and land.The people were always afraid.They wished they knew how to stop the ground from shaking.</p><p>People all over the world would like to know when an earthquake is coming.But an earthquake is almost always a surprise.Under the surface of the Earth, huge blocks of rock drift apart or slide against each other.The ground above splits apart or rumbles and shakes.</p><p>Some scientists hope to predict quakes by keeping a close watch on animals.It seems that some animals can sense an earthquake coming.In 1969, animals in a Chinese zoo began to act funny one day.Swans flew out of their pond.A panda sat down, covered its eyes with its paws, and groaned.The animals seemed to know that something was about to happen.And it did.An earthquake struck.What was it that the animals sensed? Scientists are trying to find out.</p><p>Keeping close track of the Earth&#x27;s magnetic force in earthquake areas may also help.A few years ago, in Hollister, CA, scientists kept a record of the area&#x27;s magnetic pull.For one week, the force grew stronger.Then it weakened suddenly.A day later, an earthquake struck.</p><p>It may become possible to know when and where an earthquake will happen.But it will be much harder to stop one from happening.</p><p>Many scientists think that the Earth&#x27;s covering is not smooth.They say the earth&#x27;s &quot;skin&quot; is made up of huge puzzle pieces called plates.Land and ocean floors make up these huge plates.Under the Earth&#x27;s crust  , or plates, is hot rock.The plates float on top of this rock.Sometimes the rock forces its way through the crust.What happens then? A volcano is born! More often, the rock moves and forces the plates to pull away from each other, causing earthquakes to happen.(Volcanoes and earthquakes often go together.)</p><p>Sometimes, the plates end up on top of each other.When this happens, the land above may look strange.Seen from the air, there seems to be a long scar in the Earth.This is called a fault  .The areas along faults have more earthquakes than other parts of the Earth.</p><p>For now, we&#x27;ll just have to shake along with the Earth.It goes through millions of small earthquakes every year.With luck, you won&#x27;t feel a thing!</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>When the rock forces its way through the Earth&#x27;s crust,   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">a volcano is born</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">an earthquake happens</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">a fault forms</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the Earth&#x27;s covering becomes smooth</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>A volcano forms when molten rock (magma) from beneath the Earth's surface forces its way through the Earth's crust and reaches or approaches the surface. Therefore, the statement correctly describes the formation of a volcano, making option A the correct answer. An earthquake involves sudden movement along a fault, while a fault is a fracture in the Earth's crust. The Earth's covering does not become smooth through this geological process.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high21593) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>7fdb070164a67850fd1a...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248405 · SUBGSGK_Q711596</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_GS_GK — Multidisciplinary Competitive Exam &amp; General Studies</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Competitive Exams</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Probability And Statistics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Probability And Statistics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>设二维随机变量<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>的概率密度函数为:<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x0007B;</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\"><mtext>其他</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" /></mrow></mrow></math>,则常数<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo></mrow></math>____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">2</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">3</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，对于二维随机变量<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>，其概率密度函数<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>需满足归一性，即<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222C;</mo><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\" /><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\" /><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>。\n2. 其次，我们需要计算概率密度函数在定义域内的二重积分。根据题目给定的定义域，我们有：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222C;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mo>&#x0222C;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\" /><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\" /><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>。\n3. 接着，我们计算二重积分。首先对y积分，得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\" /><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>。然后对x积分，得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\" /><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></math>。\n4. 最后，根据归一性，我们有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>，解得常数<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>4abb45effc497a4d7516...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248404 · SUBGSGK_Q711594</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_GS_GK — Multidisciplinary Competitive Exam &amp; General Studies</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Competitive Exams</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Probability And Statistics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Probability And Statistics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>独立地测量一个物理量,记每次测量的结果为<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>&#x003BC;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>&#x003B5;</mi></mrow></math>,其中<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003BC;</mi></mrow></math>是物理量的真值,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003B5;</mi></mrow></math>是测量产生的随机误差,且已知每次测量产生的随机误差都服从<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>上的均匀分布,如果取<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></math>次测量结果的算术平均值<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#x000AF;</mo></mover><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfrac><msubsup><mo>&#x02211;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></math>作为真值<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003BC;</mi></mrow></math>的近似值,用切比雪夫不等式估计<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#x000AF;</mo></mover><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>&#x003BC;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>的概率的结果:____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">不超过 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">不小于 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">不小于 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">不超过 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，我们需要知道切比雪夫不等式：对于任意随机变量X，其期望为μ，方差为σ^2，那么对于任意正数k，有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>&#x003BC;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>&#x003C3;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。\n2. 其次，我们需要计算随机误差<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003B5;</mi></mrow></math>的期望和方差。由题意知，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003B5;</mi></mrow></math>服从<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>上的均匀分布，其期望<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>&#x003B5;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>，方差<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>&#x003B5;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。\n3. 接着，我们计算<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#x000AF;</mo></mover></mrow></math>的期望和方差。由于每次测量都是独立的，所以<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#x000AF;</mo></mover><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfrac><msubsup><mo>&#x02211;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>&#x003BC;</mi></mrow></math>，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#x000AF;</mo></mover><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfrac><msubsup><mo>&#x02211;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>64</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><msubsup><mo>&#x02211;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。 \n4. 最后，我们利用切比雪夫不等式估计<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#x000AF;</mo></mover><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>&#x003BC;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>。由切比雪夫不等式，我们有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#x000AF;</mo></mover><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>&#x003BC;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#x000AF;</mo></mover><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。所以，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#x000AF;</mo></mover><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>&#x003BC;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。 因此，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#x000AF;</mo></mover><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>&#x003BC;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>的概率不小于<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>，答案是C。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>9027448a16e7706200bc...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248403 · SUBGSGK_Q711592</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_GS_GK — Multidisciplinary Competitive Exam &amp; General Studies</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Competitive Exams</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Probability And Statistics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Probability And Statistics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>设随机变量<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>的联合密度函数是:<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x0007B;</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\"><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>其他</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" /></mrow></mrow></math>则<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo></mrow></math>____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math></div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math></div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，我们需要找到常数k。为了使f(x, y)成为一个有效的联合密度函数，我们需要满足<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>。由于f(x, y)在x&gt;0和y&gt;0的区域内为非零值，我们可以将积分限改为<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>。\n2. 计算积分，得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>k</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>。解得<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>。\n3. 现在我们已经知道联合密度函数<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x0007B;</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>其他</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" /></mrow></mrow></math>。接下来，我们需要计算<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>，即在给定范围内的联合密度函数的积分：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></math>。\n4. 计算积分，得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>838729a87e8f8610fea5...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248402 · SUBAPTQUAN_Q709808</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_APT_QUANT — Quantitative Aptitude, Arithmetic, Data Interpretation &amp; Elementary Mathematics</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Middle School Mathematics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Middle School Mathematics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>已知关于x的不等式组<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x0007B;</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" /></mrow></mrow></math>恰有两个整数解，则a的取值范围为____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math></div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math></div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，我们需要解第二个不等式<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>。将其化简得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>。\n2. 接着，我们将两个不等式组合在一起，得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>且<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>。由题意，这个不等式组恰有两个整数解，因此，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>和<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>。\n3. 最后，我们需要找到a的取值范围。将这两个<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>取值代入不等式<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>，得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>和<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>。解这两个不等式，我们得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>和<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>，合并两个条件得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。由于题目要求恰有两个整数解，因此，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>。所以有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>，化简后得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>。因此，a的取值范围为<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>e397a1baf0759557bb5d...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248401 · SUBSCICHEM_Q709237</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_SCI_CHEMISTRY — Chemistry (Physical, Inorganic, Organic &amp; Analytical)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Science</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Middle School Chemistry</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Middle School Chemistry (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>取一定量的氧化铁与氧化铜的混合物，加入溶质质量分数为9.8%的稀硫酸100g，恰好完全反应生成盐和水.原混合物中氧元素的质量是____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">6.4g</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">3.2g</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">1.8g</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">1.6g</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，我们需要知道氧化铁和氧化铜与稀硫酸反应的化学方程式：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>→</mi><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>O</mi></mrow></math>；<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>O</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>→</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>O</mi></mrow></math>。根据题目描述，这两个反应都发生了，且完全反应。\n2. 其次，分析化学方程式可知氧化物中氧元素全部转变为水中的氧元素。\n3. 接着，我们需要计算生成的水的质量。设生成水的质量是x g：由方程式可以看出硫酸与生成水的关系为<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>98</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#x000D7;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#x00025;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>,解得x=1.8 g,所以水中氧元素的质量为：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1.8</mn><mi>g</mi><mo>&#x000D7;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow></math>。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>707c76d26f7eb1e3a69d...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248400 · SUBAPTQUAN_Q706814</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_APT_QUANT — Quantitative Aptitude, Arithmetic, Data Interpretation &amp; Elementary Mathematics</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> High School Mathematics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> High School Mathematics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>在矩形ABCD种，AB=1,AD=2,则点P在以点C为圆心且与BD相切的圆上，若<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>&#x02192;</mo></mover><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>&#x003BB;</mi><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#x02192;</mo></mover><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>&#x003BC;</mi><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>&#x02192;</mo></mover></mrow></math>,则<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003BB;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>&#x003BC;</mi></mrow></math>的最大值为____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">3</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">2</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，我们需要求圆的半径。BD长为<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>，圆的半径为C到BD做垂线的长度，即<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x000D7;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。\n2. 设A点为原点，AD为x轴，AB为y轴，则点P坐标需要满足的圆的参数方程可写为<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>，又有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003BB;</mi></mrow></math>和<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003BC;</mi></mrow></math>满足<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#x003BC;</mi></mrow></math>，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>&#x003BB;</mi></mrow></math>，与圆的参数方程联立可得<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003BC;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>&#x003BB;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>。\n3. 整理可得<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003BB;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>&#x003BC;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>，设<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003D5;</mi></mrow></math>满足<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#x003D5;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003D5;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>，则有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003BB;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>&#x003BC;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>&#x003D5;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>6b59858f6c56fa223d73...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248399 · SUBCSALGO_Q703898</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_CS_ALGO — Programming, Data Structures &amp; Algorithms</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Computer Architecture</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Computer Architecture (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>一个C语言程序在一台32位机器上运行，程序中定义了3个变量x、y、z，其中x和z是int型，y为short型。当x=127，y=-9时，执行赋值语句z=x+y后，x、y、z的值分别是____。</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">x=0000007FH，y=FFF9H，z=00000076H</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">x=0000007FH，y=FFF9H，z=FFFF0076H</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">x=0000007FH，y=FFF7H，z=FFFF0076H</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">x=0000007FH，y=FFF7H，z=00000076H</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. x和z为int型，说明x和z都占32位的存储空间。\r\n2. 127换成二进制为0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0111 1111，对应的十六进制为0000007FH。z进行运算后变成118，换成二进制为0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0111 0110，对应的十六进制为00000076H。\r\n3. 另外，因为y为short型，所以y所占存储空间为16位，且在计算机中使用补码表示（默认的）。-9的二进制表示为1000 0000 0000 1001，因此-9的补码表示为1111 1111 1111 0111(符号位不变，其余位取反加1)，对应的十六进制为FFF7H。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>6c87ffa825ba692f71ce...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248398 · SUBSCIPHYS_Q703315</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_SCI_PHYSICS — Physics (Classical Mechanics, Electromagnetism, Quantum, Optics &amp; Solid State)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Science</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> College Physics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> College Physics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>光子能量为0.5MeV的X射线，入射到某种物质上而发生康普顿散射．若反冲电子的能量为0.1MeV，则散射光波长的改变量Δλ与入射光波长λ_0之比值为____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">0.2</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">0.25</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">0.3</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">0.35</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，我们需要将入射光子能量和散射光子能量转换成波长。可以使用公式<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></math>，其中E表示能量，λ表示波长。入射光子能量为0.5 MeV，对应波长<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>。反冲电子能量为0.1 MeV，因此散射光子能量为0.4 MeV，对应波长<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>&#x003BB;</mi><mrow><mi>&#x02032;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>。\n2. 其次，我们计算<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x00394;</mi><mi>&#x003BB;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>&#x003BB;</mi><mrow><mi>&#x02032;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msub><mi>&#x003BB;</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>。\n3. 最后，我们要求<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>&#x00394;</mi><mi>&#x003BB;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math>。化简得到比值为0.25。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>cf3dd4df057b0e635ebf...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248397 · SUBSCIPHYS_Q703313</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_SCI_PHYSICS — Physics (Classical Mechanics, Electromagnetism, Quantum, Optics &amp; Solid State)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Science</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> College Physics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> College Physics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>有一劲度系数为k的轻弹簧，竖直放置，下端悬一质量为m的小球，开始时使弹簧为原长而小球恰好与地接触，今将弹簧上端缓慢地提起，直到小球刚能脱离地面为止，在此过程中外力作功为____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>/(4k)</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>/(3k)</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>/(2k)</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></math></div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 当小球刚好脱离地面时，弹簧的弹力与小球所受重力相等，即<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></math>，其中x表示弹簧的伸长量。\n2. 由上述方程可得，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></math>。\n3. 外力作功等于弹簧势能的增加，即<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>（因为开始时弹簧为原长，势能为0）。\n4. 将第2步中得到的x代入第3步的公式，得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mi>k</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>71fbf27eda41bfaa0e9b...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248396 · SUBGSINDIA_Q702759</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">COUNTRY_LOCAL: India</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_GS_INDIAN_ECONOMY — Indian Economy, Economic Development, Planning, Budgeting &amp; Social Sector</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Civil Services &amp; GS</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> College Economics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> College Economics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>已知一垄断企业成本函数为TC=5Q2+20Q+10，产品的需求函数为Q=140-P。利润最大化的产量为____。</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">10</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">5</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">3</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">15</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，垄断企业的利润最大化产量是当边际收益MR等于边际成本MC时。因此，我们需要求出该企业的边际收益和边际成本函数。\n2. 其次，求出总收益TR。<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>140</mn><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>。\n3. 接着，通过总收益TR求出边际收益MR函数，即<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#x00394;</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#x00394;</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>140</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi></mrow></math>。\n4. 最后，通过成本函数TC求出边际成本MC函数，即<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#x00394;</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#x00394;</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>Q</mi></mrow></math>。\n5. 根据上述计算，我们将边际收益函数和边际成本函数相等，即<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>140</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>Q</mi></mrow></math>，解得<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math>。因此，利润最大化的产量为10。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>f8bdcafce5147c6c1de4...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248395 · SUBGSINDIA_Q702758</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">COUNTRY_LOCAL: India</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_GS_INDIAN_ECONOMY — Indian Economy, Economic Development, Planning, Budgeting &amp; Social Sector</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Civil Services &amp; GS</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> College Economics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> College Economics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>考虑以下小型开放经济的数据：Y=1000，C=700，G=150，I=250-1000r*。如果世界利率为5%，那么小型开放经济的净出口为____。</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">50</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">-50</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">150</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">-150</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，小型开放经济的净出口公式：NX = S - I，其中NX表示净出口，S表示储蓄，I表示投资。\n2. 其次，根据国民账户恒等式，Y = C + I + G + NX，可以得到S = Y - C - G。将数据代入得到S = 150。\n3. 接着，根据题目中的数据计算投资，I = 250 - 1000r*，其中r*表示世界利率。将r* = 5%代入得到I = 200。\n4. 最后，计算净出口。将步骤2和步骤3的结果代入净出口公式，得到NX = S - I = 150 - 200 = -50。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>6b41dc62f62ad67686bc...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248394 · SUBSCICHEM_Q702506</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_SCI_CHEMISTRY — Chemistry (Physical, Inorganic, Organic &amp; Analytical)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Science</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> College Chemistry</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> College Chemistry (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>下列物质加入电池负极溶液中，使<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>/<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></math>-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></msup></mrow></math>/<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>组成的原电池电动势增大的是____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></math>固体</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Zn粒</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>S</mi></mrow></math>溶液</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></math>固体</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，我们需要了解<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>/<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></math>-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></msup></mrow></math>/<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>组成的原电池，其中<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>/<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></math>是负极，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></msup></mrow></math>/<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>是正极。\n2. 其次，增大正极的电极电势或降低负极的电极电势可使电池电动势增大。显然，降低负极氧化型的浓度能使负极的电极电势减小。\n3. 分析选项： (A)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></math>固体，(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></math>粒和(D)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></math>固体，加入后不会改变电池的还原反应和氧化反应，因此不会使电池电动势增大；(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>S</mi></mrow></math>溶液，加入<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>使大部分<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>被沉淀下来，降低了<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>的浓度，负极电势减小。\n4. 根据以上分析，加入<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>S</mi></mrow></math>溶液可以使<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>/<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></math>-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></msup></mrow></math>/<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>组成的原电池电动势增大。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>52a56bc6152928581e1e...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248393 · SUBAPTQUAN_Q700493</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_APT_QUANT — Quantitative Aptitude, Arithmetic, Data Interpretation &amp; Elementary Mathematics</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Advanced Mathematics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Advanced Mathematics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>求定积分：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo></mrow></math>____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，我们观察到积分中的<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>，可以首先考虑进行变换。有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>。\n2. 其次，考虑使用换元积分法进行求解。令<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>u</mi></mrow></math>。\n3. 接着，我们需要将积分区间进行变换。当<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>时，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>；当<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>时，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>，因此积分区间变为<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math>。\n4. 将换元后的<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>代入原式，得到：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mi>u</mi><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mi>u</mi><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mi>u</mi></mrow></math>。\n5. 再次使用换元积分法，令<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></math>，当<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>时，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>；当<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>时，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>，因此，积分区间变为<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mfrac><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math>。\n6. 最后，将换元后的<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow></math>代入第4步的表达式，得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mi>u</mi><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mi>sin</mi><mi>t</mi><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mi>sin</mi><mi>t</mi><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>t</mi><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>ae6f08bf65d69ee9a506...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248392 · SUBAPTQUAN_Q700492</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_APT_QUANT — Quantitative Aptitude, Arithmetic, Data Interpretation &amp; Elementary Mathematics</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Advanced Mathematics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Advanced Mathematics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>求不定积分：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></math></div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></math></div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，我们可以观察到积分中有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>和<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>两部分，我们可以尝试使用分部积分法求解。\n2. 其次，对于原式<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>。\n3. 接着，继续使用分部积分法计算<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>。<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></math>。\n4. 然后，继续使用分部积分法计算<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>。<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>ln</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>&#x00064;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>ln</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>。\n5. 最后，带入第3、4步的计算结果可以得到，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></math>。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>87424a0d150bb52df9a7...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248391 · SUBAPTQUAN_Q700491</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_APT_QUANT — Quantitative Aptitude, Arithmetic, Data Interpretation &amp; Elementary Mathematics</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Advanced Mathematics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Advanced Mathematics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>求<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></math>在<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>&#x00065;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>&#x00065;</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mrow></math>点的曲率半径____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>&#x00065;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>&#x00065;</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>&#x00065;</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>&#x00065;</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math></div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，对原方程两边取<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></math>指数，可以有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></math>。\n2. 其次，对方程两边同时求导：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。于是，当<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>，有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。\n3. 其次，对<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>两边同时求导并化简，有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>&#x02033;</mi></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。于是，当<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>时，有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>&#x02033;</mi></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。\n4. 最后，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></math>在<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>处的曲率<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></msub><mi>K</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>&#x02033;</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>。因此，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></math>在<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>处的曲率半径为<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>5b9a06fe04e3b660f6ce...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248390 · SUBAPTQUAN_Q700490</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_APT_QUANT — Quantitative Aptitude, Arithmetic, Data Interpretation &amp; Elementary Mathematics</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Advanced Mathematics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Advanced Mathematics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>求极限：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x022EF;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo>&#x022EF;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x0003D;</mo></mrow></math>____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，利用等差数列求和公式分析题目中表达式的第n项，可以发现：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo>&#x022EF;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>，其中<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>。\n2. 其次，将第1步中的表达式代入原式，有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x022EF;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo>&#x022EF;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x022EF;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。\n3. 最后，可以发现第2步中不同项之间的分子和分母存在重叠，化简后可以得到<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mo>&#x0221E;</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>，所以极限值为<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>04114d3336e344cf41ae...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248389 · SUBAPTQUAN_Q700489</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_APT_QUANT — Quantitative Aptitude, Arithmetic, Data Interpretation &amp; Elementary Mathematics</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: Global &amp; National Competitive Exam (ceval-exam) (2021-2024)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Academic &amp; Professional Exam Benchmark · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Advanced Mathematics</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Advanced Mathematics (ZH Exam Paper)</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>求极限：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo></mrow></math>____</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">-1</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">0</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">2</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>1. 首先，观察表达式，对上述表达式进行拆分，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>\n2. 其次，计算<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></math>。有命题：设<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>在<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>的邻域内可导，且<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>；又设<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>，且对<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x0007C;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mi>&#x003B4;</mi></mrow></math>有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02260;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>成立，则：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></math>。对于<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></math>，令<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>。于是有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>。\n3. 接着，计算<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>。有命题：设<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>，函数<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>在<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>的邻域附近解析，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02262;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>，则：<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>。对于<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>，令<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>，且<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>，则有<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02192;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>。\n4. 最后，<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>。</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> HIGH_CONFIDENCE_SAFE (MIT 52-Subject University &amp; Professional Exam PYQs) · ceval/ceval-exam</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>952869f1966b062b27b4...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248388 · SUBLANGENG_Q495803</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_EFBD26114C50 (Question 3 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high20162)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_EFBD26114C50 · Question 3 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A new study has been carried to test the role of story telling in lowering blood pressure. Dr. Thomas Houston, a professor of the University of Massachusetts Medical School, led a group of scientists that investigated how pre-recorded videos of hypertension   patients&#x27; talking about their medical histories helped another group of patients with high blood pressure to control their condition over several months.</p><p>Houston was surprised by their studies that suggested that communication can be a powerful tool in medicine. They showed that those who had had similar experiences, when talking to someone with a similar background, could help change their behavior to become healthier. Hypertension is difficult to control, since it is dependent on diet, exercise and mental state. Medical treatments with drugs, and lifestyle therapies  have been  ly ineffective because people find it hard to follow those medical requirements.</p><p>In the test, his team carefully chose their story-tellers from 230 members of a patients&#x27; community with whom they could most easily relate. Next, they divided their study population into two groups. One received three interactive   DVDs containing the tellers&#x27; stories of their experiences in living with and treating their hypertension. The other were given educational discs on an unrelated health topic. The study volunteers reported that they had listened to the DVDs, and after three months, those who heard the stories of the hypertensive patients lowered their blood pressure.</p><p>While the study did not  _ how the story-telling influenced the patients&#x27; behavior, Houston suspects that watching patients of similar backgrounds who had a similar medical experience helped to motivate them to seek medical help to their hypertension. They found that after six months the difference in blood pressure between those who watched the story-tellers and those who observed the unrelated videos remained, suggesting that the story-telling continued to have an effect.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Which of the following could be the best title of the text?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">The stories of some hypertension patients.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Medical treatments of blood pressure.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Storytelling may help lower blood pressure.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Suggestions about how to lower blood pressure.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The central idea of the passage is that storytelling and communication between patients with similar experiences may help control high blood pressure. The study examined how recorded personal medical histories influenced other hypertension patients over several months. Therefore, option C best captures both the research method and its potential benefit. Option A is too narrow, B incorrectly focuses on conventional medical treatments, and D suggests general lifestyle advice rather than patient storytelling.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high20162) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>cf9cf10d0ea03fcb2af9...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248387 · SUBLANGENG_Q495802</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_EFBD26114C50 (Question 2 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high20162)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_EFBD26114C50 · Question 2 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A new study has been carried to test the role of story telling in lowering blood pressure. Dr. Thomas Houston, a professor of the University of Massachusetts Medical School, led a group of scientists that investigated how pre-recorded videos of hypertension   patients&#x27; talking about their medical histories helped another group of patients with high blood pressure to control their condition over several months.</p><p>Houston was surprised by their studies that suggested that communication can be a powerful tool in medicine. They showed that those who had had similar experiences, when talking to someone with a similar background, could help change their behavior to become healthier. Hypertension is difficult to control, since it is dependent on diet, exercise and mental state. Medical treatments with drugs, and lifestyle therapies  have been  ly ineffective because people find it hard to follow those medical requirements.</p><p>In the test, his team carefully chose their story-tellers from 230 members of a patients&#x27; community with whom they could most easily relate. Next, they divided their study population into two groups. One received three interactive   DVDs containing the tellers&#x27; stories of their experiences in living with and treating their hypertension. The other were given educational discs on an unrelated health topic. The study volunteers reported that they had listened to the DVDs, and after three months, those who heard the stories of the hypertensive patients lowered their blood pressure.</p><p>While the study did not  _ how the story-telling influenced the patients&#x27; behavior, Houston suspects that watching patients of similar backgrounds who had a similar medical experience helped to motivate them to seek medical help to their hypertension. They found that after six months the difference in blood pressure between those who watched the story-tellers and those who observed the unrelated videos remained, suggesting that the story-telling continued to have an effect.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Houston was surprised to find that   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">hypertension is really difficult to control</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">communication has some medical effects</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">medical treatments have no effect at all</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">people don&#x27;t follow the medical requirements</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage states that Houston was surprised by the study's findings, which suggested that communication could be a powerful tool in medicine. The videos demonstrated that patients sharing similar medical experiences could positively influence others' ability to control hypertension. Thus, option B correctly expresses the unexpected medical value of communication. Options A, C and D introduce claims about disease severity, treatment ineffectiveness and patient noncompliance that the passage does not establish.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high20162) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>c18342d572096f81f476...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248386 · SUBLANGENG_Q495801</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_EFBD26114C50 (Question 1 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high20162)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_EFBD26114C50 · Question 1 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A new study has been carried to test the role of story telling in lowering blood pressure. Dr. Thomas Houston, a professor of the University of Massachusetts Medical School, led a group of scientists that investigated how pre-recorded videos of hypertension   patients&#x27; talking about their medical histories helped another group of patients with high blood pressure to control their condition over several months.</p><p>Houston was surprised by their studies that suggested that communication can be a powerful tool in medicine. They showed that those who had had similar experiences, when talking to someone with a similar background, could help change their behavior to become healthier. Hypertension is difficult to control, since it is dependent on diet, exercise and mental state. Medical treatments with drugs, and lifestyle therapies  have been  ly ineffective because people find it hard to follow those medical requirements.</p><p>In the test, his team carefully chose their story-tellers from 230 members of a patients&#x27; community with whom they could most easily relate. Next, they divided their study population into two groups. One received three interactive   DVDs containing the tellers&#x27; stories of their experiences in living with and treating their hypertension. The other were given educational discs on an unrelated health topic. The study volunteers reported that they had listened to the DVDs, and after three months, those who heard the stories of the hypertensive patients lowered their blood pressure.</p><p>While the study did not  _ how the story-telling influenced the patients&#x27; behavior, Houston suspects that watching patients of similar backgrounds who had a similar medical experience helped to motivate them to seek medical help to their hypertension. They found that after six months the difference in blood pressure between those who watched the story-tellers and those who observed the unrelated videos remained, suggesting that the story-telling continued to have an effect.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>We can learn from the text that the pre-recorded videos   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">tell medical histories of hypertension patients</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">introduce some medical treatments of hypertension</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">introduce a good lifestyle for hypertensive patients</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">tell scientific discoveries of the scientist group</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage explicitly states that the pre-recorded videos featured hypertension patients talking about their medical histories. These personal accounts were shared with other patients to demonstrate how communication could help manage high blood pressure. Therefore, option A accurately identifies the videos' content. Option B incorrectly suggests that the videos presented medical treatments, while C and D refer to lifestyle advice and scientific discoveries, neither of which is supported by the passage.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high20162) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>dd2e291e2505e8e74fa5...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248385 · SUBLANGENG_Q495800</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_EBDDC0287740 (Question 3 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high24133)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_EBDDC0287740 · Question 3 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>School is out for the summer in some areas, and for many children, that means weeks of sleeping in late, trips to the swimming pool or hours spent in front of the TV. These months of inactivity--- away from the daily tiring things of school--- are something that young people look forward to, but it can have a detrimental influence on the knowledge they have.</p><p>Studies have shown that children lose a lot in math skills during the summer months. Children who spend little time learning experience a much greater amount of learning loss than those who often take part in summer programs.</p><p>So when school starts again in the fall, teachers often have to spend several weeks reteaching children material that they have forgotten.</p><p>Experts suggest that parents make sure the summer months are a time of continued learning. For example, they suggest that lunch time is good time to improve a child&#x27;s spoken skills, simply through conversation. A trip to the supermarket can be an opportunity to improve a child&#x27;s math skills by having him or her add up the cost of food. And there is no better way to prevent learning loss than by having a child read every day.</p><p>Fortunately, there are many programs that can help parents. The best place to start is at your local library. Most libraries have summer reading programs that are filled with fun activities. A. strong musical education also improves learning. Find out summer music camps in your area.</p><p>We think that children should have fun during the summer break, but it should not be a vacation from learning. We strongly suggest parents should take advantage of the many educational opportunities available for their children during the coming weeks.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>might be most interested in this passage.</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Students</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Teachers</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Parents</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Reporters</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Parents are likely the most interested audience for this passage, as they are directly responsible for managing their children's summer activities and academic development. The passage highlights the benefits of summer programs and the risks of summer learning loss, providing crucial guidance for parents seeking to support their children's education during the break.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high24133) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>1dba170ceab863a8b788...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248384 · SUBLANGENG_Q495799</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_EBDDC0287740 (Question 2 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high24133)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_EBDDC0287740 · Question 2 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>School is out for the summer in some areas, and for many children, that means weeks of sleeping in late, trips to the swimming pool or hours spent in front of the TV. These months of inactivity--- away from the daily tiring things of school--- are something that young people look forward to, but it can have a detrimental influence on the knowledge they have.</p><p>Studies have shown that children lose a lot in math skills during the summer months. Children who spend little time learning experience a much greater amount of learning loss than those who often take part in summer programs.</p><p>So when school starts again in the fall, teachers often have to spend several weeks reteaching children material that they have forgotten.</p><p>Experts suggest that parents make sure the summer months are a time of continued learning. For example, they suggest that lunch time is good time to improve a child&#x27;s spoken skills, simply through conversation. A trip to the supermarket can be an opportunity to improve a child&#x27;s math skills by having him or her add up the cost of food. And there is no better way to prevent learning loss than by having a child read every day.</p><p>Fortunately, there are many programs that can help parents. The best place to start is at your local library. Most libraries have summer reading programs that are filled with fun activities. A. strong musical education also improves learning. Find out summer music camps in your area.</p><p>We think that children should have fun during the summer break, but it should not be a vacation from learning. We strongly suggest parents should take advantage of the many educational opportunities available for their children during the coming weeks.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Which of the following is true?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">It isn&#x27;t good for children to have fun in summer.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Children will get bored with reading programs</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Summer programs can be helpful for children.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Teachers needn&#x27;t help children review lessons.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>According to the passage, children who participate in summer programs experience less learning loss compared to those who do not. This indicates that summer programs are beneficial and helpful in mitigating the academic decline that occurs during summer break. Therefore, option C is the correct statement, while the other options are either unsupported or contradicted by the text.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high24133) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>d096537fa08a84eff191...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248383 · SUBLANGENG_Q495798</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_EBDDC0287740 (Question 1 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high24133)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_EBDDC0287740 · Question 1 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>School is out for the summer in some areas, and for many children, that means weeks of sleeping in late, trips to the swimming pool or hours spent in front of the TV. These months of inactivity--- away from the daily tiring things of school--- are something that young people look forward to, but it can have a detrimental influence on the knowledge they have.</p><p>Studies have shown that children lose a lot in math skills during the summer months. Children who spend little time learning experience a much greater amount of learning loss than those who often take part in summer programs.</p><p>So when school starts again in the fall, teachers often have to spend several weeks reteaching children material that they have forgotten.</p><p>Experts suggest that parents make sure the summer months are a time of continued learning. For example, they suggest that lunch time is good time to improve a child&#x27;s spoken skills, simply through conversation. A trip to the supermarket can be an opportunity to improve a child&#x27;s math skills by having him or her add up the cost of food. And there is no better way to prevent learning loss than by having a child read every day.</p><p>Fortunately, there are many programs that can help parents. The best place to start is at your local library. Most libraries have summer reading programs that are filled with fun activities. A. strong musical education also improves learning. Find out summer music camps in your area.</p><p>We think that children should have fun during the summer break, but it should not be a vacation from learning. We strongly suggest parents should take advantage of the many educational opportunities available for their children during the coming weeks.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Children lose a lot in learning in the summer break because they_.</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">do homework before the TV</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">stay up late at night</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">visit the swimming pool</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">spend little time learning</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage explicitly states that children who spend little time learning experience a much greater amount of learning loss during the summer. Option D directly reflects this cause-and-effect relationship. Options A, B, and C describe typical summer activities mentioned in the text, but they are not identified as the primary cause of learning loss, which is specifically tied to the lack of learning activities.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high24133) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>4b2d409f12ee661354b2...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    "}
